  "observableConclusions": [
    "VMware firmware and motherboard layout are independent profile axes; acpi plus BIOS is explicitly unsupported",
    "Both tested VMware layouts still exposed a 440BX/PIIX4 chipset; acpi changed the host-bridge topology rather than changing the guest to Q35",
    "A VMware BIOS guest may enumerate and exercise passthrough endpoints while leaving a 2 GiB BAR unassigned",
    "SeaBIOS is not a behavioral substitute for VMware BIOS: tested QEMU SeaBIOS profiles allocated the same 2 GiB BAR above 4 GiB",
    "Stock QEMU has no single argument set that simultaneously preserves the VMware legacy chipset identity, VMware PCIe-root-port topology, VMware acpi multi-root topology, and exact high-MMIO base",
    "MMIO planning must include every auxiliary and bridge resource plus alignment padding; target BAR sizes alone are insufficient"
  ],
